# Print key material or a fingerprint from a key generated fresh each run, so no fixture can
# pin them. Committing a private key to reproduce them would be worse. Verified by hand in
# the sandbox against a generated key, where each printed the expected shape.
View the public key
Show a key's fingerprint
Start ssh-agent and add a key
List keys currently held by the agent

# Needs the public internet and a third party's server. Verified by hand from a networked
# Debian trixie box.
Pre-populate known_hosts without logging in
Test key-based auth against a known real host

# Needs a real host to connect to; the trace is also full of per-connection detail. Verified
# by hand between two sandbox containers with sshd running.
Get a step-by-step trace of the connection

# The "code" here is an ssh_config block, not a shell command. Its output comes from `ssh -G`
# after the block is in place. Verified by hand with the block written to ~/.ssh/config.
Enable connection sharing for a host
